---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import ReviewNotice from '../components/ReviewNotice.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';

/* The PAIA manual is a statutory obligation, not a nice-to-have. Section 51 of
   the Promotion of Access to Information Act requires every private body to
   compile one, keep it current, and make it available — including on its
   website if it has one. POPIA amended what it must contain.

   This page is the shape of a compliant manual with the facts that have not
   been supplied left visible. It is not yet a compliant manual. */
---

<Base
  title="PAIA manual | TGM Group"
  description="TGM Group's manual in terms of section 51 of the Promotion of Access to Information Act, including how to request access to records."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'PAIA manual', href: '/paia/' }])]}
>
  <PageHero
    accent="navy"
    title="PAIA manual"
    lead="Our manual under section 51 of the Promotion of Access to Information Act 2 of 2000, as amended by POPIA. It explains what records we hold and how to request access to them."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <ReviewNotice>
          The particulars, the information officer and the registered address
          below are now complete and taken from the CIPC registration
          certificate and the Information Regulator certificate. The records
          schedule in section 4 still needs confirming against what the
          business actually keeps, and an attorney should review the whole
          document before it is relied on.
        </ReviewNotice>

        <h2>1. Particulars of the private body</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Registered name:</strong> {site.legalName}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Trading as:</strong> {site.name}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Registration number:</strong> {site.registrationNumber}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Date of registration:</strong> {site.registrationDate}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Company type:</strong> {site.companyType}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Physical address:</strong>
            {
              site.address && (
                <>
                  {site.address.street}, {site.address.locality},{' '}
                  {site.address.region}, {site.address.postalCode},{' '}
                  {site.address.country}
                </>
              )
            }
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Postal address:</strong> As above.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Telephone:</strong>
            <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Email:</strong>
            <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Website:</strong> {site.url}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Directors:</strong> {site.directors.join(', ')}
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Information officer</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Information officer:</strong> {site.informationOfficer.name}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Appointed:</strong> {site.informationOfficer.appointed}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Registered with the Information Regulator:</strong>{' '}
            {site.informationOfficer.regulatorRegistrationDate}, registration
            number {site.informationOfficer.regulatorRegistrationNumber}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact:</strong>
            <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, or by post to the
            registered address in section 1. Please mark correspondence for the
            attention of the information officer.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Registration with the Information Regulator is complete. No deputy
          information officer has been designated.
          <span class="placeholder">
            [Confirm whether a deputy is required given current headcount]
          </span>
        </p>

        <h2>3. The Information Regulator's guide</h2>
        <p>
          The Information Regulator has compiled a guide explaining how to use
          PAIA. It is published in each official language and you do not need to
          ask us for it:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://inforegulator.org.za/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/PAIA-Guide-English_20210905.pdf"
              rel="noopener">Guide on how to use PAIA (English, PDF)</a>. Other
            languages are on the Regulator's
            <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za/paia/" rel="noopener">PAIA page</a>.
          </li>
          <li>The Information Regulator (South Africa), PO Box 31533, Braamfontein, Johannesburg, 2017</li>
          <li>Email: <a href="mailto:inforeg@justice.gov.za">inforeg@justice.gov.za</a></li>
          <li>Website: <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" rel="noopener">inforegulator.org.za</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Records held</h2>
        <p>
          A complete manual must list the categories of records we hold, and
          state which are automatically available and which require a request.
          The categories below are indicative and must be confirmed against
          what the business actually keeps.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Company records:</strong> incorporation documents, statutory
            registers, minutes and resolutions
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Financial records:</strong> annual financial statements,
            tax returns, invoices, banking records
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Client records:</strong> engagement agreements,
            correspondence, deliverables, working papers
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Personnel records:</strong> contracts, payroll, statutory
            returns
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Enquiry records:</strong> submissions through this website,
            as described in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <span class="placeholder">[Confirm and complete this schedule]</span>
        </p>

        <h2>5. Records available without a formal request</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing has been published under section 52 of PAIA. Our privacy
          policy, terms of use and this manual are freely available on this
          website.
        </p>

        <h2>6. How to request access</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            Complete the prescribed request form, Form 2 of the PAIA
            Regulations:
            <a
              href="https://inforegulator.org.za/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/InfoRegSA-PAIA-Form02-Reg7.pdf"
              rel="noopener">Request for Access to Record (PDF)</a>. A request
            on anything other than the prescribed form may be refused.
          </li>
          <li>
            Send it to the information officer at
            <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or the postal
            address above.
          </li>
          <li>
            Provide enough detail to identify the record and to identify
            yourself, and state the form of access you want.
          </li>
          <li>
            If the request is in the public interest or relates to your own
            personal information, say so and explain why.
          </li>
          <li>
            Pay the prescribed request fee where one applies. Access fees are
            payable before the record is released.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          We will respond within 30 days. That period may be extended once, by
          up to 30 days, where the request is for a large number of records or
          requires a search through records held elsewhere. We will tell you in
          writing if that happens.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Grounds for refusal</h2>
        <p>
          We may refuse access where PAIA requires or permits it, including
          where release would unreasonably disclose someone else's personal
          information, breach a duty of confidence owed to a client, disclose
          commercial information belonging to a third party, or where the record
          is privileged in legal proceedings. If we refuse, we will tell you in
          writing which ground we relied on.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are unhappy with our decision, you may lodge a complaint with
          the Information Regulator using
          <a
            href="https://inforegulator.org.za/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/InfoRegSA-PAIA-Form05-Reg10-1.pdf"
            rel="noopener">Form 5</a>, or apply to a court. You do not need our
          permission to do either.
          <span class="placeholder">
            [Attorney to confirm the remedies available against a private body
            and whether an internal appeal applies]
          </span>
        </p>

        <h2>8. Fees</h2>
        <p>
          The request and access fees prescribed under PAIA apply. The current
          schedule is published by the Information Regulator.
          <span class="placeholder">[Confirm current fee schedule]</span>
        </p>

        <h2>9. Availability of this manual</h2>
        <p>
          This manual is available on this website, and on request at our
          registered address, at no charge.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our information officer is registered with the Information Regulator
          under registration number{' '}
          {site.informationOfficer.regulatorRegistrationNumber}. Registering the
          information officer and submitting this manual to the Regulator are
          separate steps.
          <span class="placeholder">
            [Confirm whether the manual itself has been submitted to the
            Information Regulator]
          </span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Last updated:</strong>
          <span class="placeholder">[Date of legal sign-off]</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
